## STEP 1 — UPPAAL Models

### File: `assets/CS10_Drone/V1_PT.xml`

Template name: `SprayingDronePT`

**Clocks:** `t_flight`, `t_spray`, `t_battery`, `t_zone`

**Locations (8 total):**
```
GROUNDED          — drone at base, battery fully charged
NAVIGATING        — in-flight, heading to next spray zone
ENTERING_ZONE     — approaching spray zone boundary
SPRAYING          — active spray, covering current hectare
EXITING_ZONE      — spray complete, leaving zone
RETURNING         — mission complete or battery low, returning to base
RECHARGING        — at base, battery recharging
FAULT             — system fault (spray nozzle, GPS, battery)
```

**Transitions (consistent with Example 2 guard conditions):**

```
GROUNDED -> NAVIGATING
  trigger: takeoff!
  guard:   t_battery <= 0    [fresh battery]
  reset:   t_flight := 0, t_battery := 0

NAVIGATING -> ENTERING_ZONE
  trigger: enter_zone!
  guard:   t_flight >= 2 && t_flight <= 30
  invariant: t_flight <= 30, reset: t_zone := 0

ENTERING_ZONE -> SPRAYING
  trigger: spray!
  guard:   t_zone >= 1
           [Example 2: consumption(current_hectare) <= 50]
  reset:   t_spray := 0

SPRAYING -> EXITING_ZONE
  trigger: exit_zone!
  guard:   t_spray >= 5 && t_spray <= 20
           [Example 2: covered(current_hectare)]
           [ISO 16119-4: minimum spray time for coverage uniformity]
  invariant: t_spray <= 20, reset: t_zone := 0

EXITING_ZONE -> NAVIGATING
  trigger: tau
  guard:   t_zone >= 1, reset: t_flight := 0

EXITING_ZONE -> RETURNING
  trigger: return_base!
  guard:   t_battery >= 450
           [EASA 2019/947: return when approaching battery limit]

NAVIGATING -> RETURNING
  trigger: shutoff!
  guard:   t_battery >= 450
           [Example 2: total_consumption <= battery_capacity AND covered]
  reset:   t_flight := 0

RETURNING -> RECHARGING
  trigger: land!
  guard:   t_flight >= 2, reset: t_battery := 0

RECHARGING -> GROUNDED
  trigger: recharge_complete!
  guard:   t_battery >= 60
  invariant: t_battery <= 120

ANY -> FAULT
  trigger: fault_detected!
  guard:   t_battery <= 3
  (from SPRAYING, NAVIGATING)

FAULT -> RETURNING
  trigger: fault_return!
  guard:   (no guard)
```

