## STEP 4 — Misalignment Variants

### Variant A — Consumption Limit Drift
`dt_thresh_drift.interp`: Change `apply!` to fire at
`consumption(1) > 60` instead of `<= 50`. This violates the EPPO
application rate limit and means the DT permits spray applications
that exceed the EU 2009/128 regulatory threshold.
Z3 must confirm NOT ENTAILED for:
`Δ |= I_PT(spray!) ↔ (consumption(1) > 60)`

### Variant B — Ontology Evolution (RQ1)

`domain_v2.ont`: Apply Definition 7 exactly as described in the paper:
- **Condition I:** Add `sort Motor`, `fun rpm : Motor -> Real`
- **Condition II:** Tighten `battery_capacity` from 500 to 450
  (models battery degradation after 200 cycles — exactly the example
  discussed in Section IV of the paper)
- **Condition III:** Update `shutoff!` to
  `(and (<= total_consumption 450) (covered 1))`

The benchmark runner must verify:
1. `domain_v2.ont |= domain.ont` (Theorem 1 Condition II)
2. Alignment preserved under `domain_v2.ont`
3. A context in which `total_consumption = 460` was valid under
   `domain.ont` is correctly rejected under `domain_v2.ont`

