## STEP 5 — Benchmark Runner

### File: `benchmark/run_CS10.cpp`

Follow the structure of `benchmark/run_CS1.cpp`. This runner must
additionally include an explicit validation section that prints:

```
=== Paper Example Validation ===
Checking: Δ |= I_PT(spray!) ↔ I_DT(apply!)     ... [ENTAILED / NOT ENTAILED]
Checking: Δ |= I_PT(shutoff!) ↔ I_DT(power_down!) ... [ENTAILED / NOT ENTAILED]
Expected: both ENTAILED (per Section VII of paper)
[PASS / FAIL]
```

If either check returns NOT ENTAILED, the implementation has a bug —
either in the ontology, interpretation, or SMT checker. This is the
ground truth validation for the entire SemAlign tool.

The syntactic bisimulation baseline (Run 2) must also print:
```
Syntactic bisimulation on (spray! vs apply!): NOT ALIGNED
[This is CORRECT — labels differ. Semantic alignment is needed.]
```

This makes the RQ2 point visually explicit in the output.